 ## Overview
-Fisheye Distortion Correction eliminates the visual bowing of flat surfaces in ray-cast scenes caused by using raw Euclidean ray lengths for perspective projection [S1, unofficial]. It replaces the naive distance with the perpendicular distance to the projection plane, ensuring that a flat wall renders as a straight line across the entire field of view [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Sky Gradient](1262-sky-gradient.md) or [Arcball Camera](1639-arcball-camera.md) which define viewing geometry, this method specifically corrects the depth value used for screen-space projection in planar scenes.
