 ## Background
-The fisheye effect in ray casting was identified as a geometric artifact where naive Euclidean distances cause flat walls to appear bowed [S1, unofficial]. The correction method, multiplying by $\cos(\delta)$, is a standard technique in ray casting tutorials and implementations to maintain visual fidelity for planar geometry [S1, unofficial]. Angular fisheye lenses, which support wider fields of view with reduced distortion, were developed for interactive volume rendering and virtual tours [S2].
